// Generated by the time stretcher's records probe; do not edit by hand, and never rewrite it with
// ./dbt test --update unit (no spec hands these arrays to golden::record()).
//
// Each array holds a contract's inputs and the legacy's results, as docs/dev/time_stretcher_contracts.md names them.
// Two probes wrote them, each applied to a scratch worktree of the legacy code:
// - The first half's (hop tuning, the planner, the aligner, the crossfader, the cache tail and the perc analysis),
//   logged at every call over the goldens (the sample/ts_*, sample/timestretch and every golden-synth case, and every
//   render-song gate recorded in songs.json), generated inputs (the *Sweep arrays) and fault injection (the *Faults
//   arrays). P2's records, and the analysis arrays, are the pitch shifter's shared SlopeFollower run on the words the
//   legacy fill read (decision 6 of docs/dev/time_stretcher_design.md); P3's bytes are the legacy's.
// - The second half's (the hop scheduler, the heads, position, loop, exit and cache write, section 5's reservations
//   and the read head), logged over the same goldens with the byte-depth cases added, sweeps of Q2 and Q3, and fault
//   injection at the seat, the chunk walks, the allocations, an eviction between calls and a forced cull.
//
// Frame windows hold, for each frame of [first_frame, last_frame] and each channel, the unmasked 32-bit word the
// legacy read for that sample: its top bytes are the sample and its low bytes the bytes before it, the word's
// read origin being the sample's top byte less three. resident_until is the first frame, in the play direction, that
// was not resident (INT32_MAX when none).
//
// The read head's records hold raw bytes instead: each chunk image is the memory of one chunk a call touched, from
// first_offset (chunk-relative, negative into the slack before the payload) on, a straddling frame's trailing bytes
// included. A HeadRecord is the legacy reader: chunk_index -1 when it holds no chunk; chunk_offset the byte offset in
// its chunk of the frame its cursor stands at; zero_taps its count of zero taps once ended; taps its window, 16 left
// then 16 right, newest first. A native read's kernel is 0: it reads none.
//
// Left unpinned: the perc store's third chunk (P1, P5) has no array, as no golden has a source over 2^23 frames.
// No golden reaches these quirks, whose kQuirkReach entries are empty: R2, R10.
